IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa23-nouns.l4: the types that more than one coa23 module needs (DECLARE only; no rules, no #EVAL, no #ASSERT).
-- Every name begins with the label of the section that first needs it, as the keel's naming rule says.
--
-- The core's `Party` has Registrar, Company, Director and so on, but no "any person", no individual who delivers a
-- document, and no officer-or-employee of an authorised corporate service provider. Rules whose party is one of those
-- use the person type declared here; rules whose party is the registrar use the core's `Party` and
-- `Action of a party`. The constructors wanted in the core are listed in NEEDS-CORE.md.

-- src:14905 | (1) There shall continue to be—
-- src:14906 | (a) a registrar of companies for England and Wales,
-- src:14907 | (b) a registrar of companies for Scotland, and
-- src:14908 | (c) a registrar of companies for Northern Ireland.
@ref s 1060(1) The registrar (src:14905-14908)
DECLARE `s 1060 registrar of companies` IS ONE OF
    `s 1060(1)(a) the registrar of companies for England and Wales`
    `s 1060(1)(b) the registrar of companies for Scotland`
    `s 1060(1)(c) the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland`

-- src:14980 | Any person may require the registrar to provide him with a copy of any certificate of incorporation of a company, signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's seal.
-- src:15001 | (1) An individual may not deliver a document to the registrar on their own behalf unless—
-- src:15030 | (1) An individual who is a disqualified person may not deliver documents to the registrar on their own behalf or on behalf of another.
-- src:15324 | (1) Any person may inspect the register.
-- src:15332 | (1) Any person may require a copy of any material on the register that is available for public inspection.
-- src:15458 | (1) A copy provided under section 1086 must be certified by the registrar as a true copy if the applicant expressly requests such certification.
@ref ss 1065, 1067A, 1067B, 1085, 1086 and 1091(1): the person who asks the registrar for something or delivers a document (src:14980 src:15001 src:15030 src:15324 src:15332 src:15458)
DECLARE `s 1065 person dealing with the registrar` IS ONE OF
    `s 1065 any person`
    `s 1067A an individual who delivers a document to the registrar`

-- What such a person does. Each constructor carries the facts a rule about the act needs, so that a #TRACE event
-- can say whether the condition the text attaches to the act was met when it was done.
DECLARE `s 1065 act of a person dealing with the registrar` IS ONE OF
    `s 1065 require a copy of a certificate of incorporation`
    `s 1067A deliver a document on their own behalf`
        HAS `s 1067A the individual's identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN
            `s 1067A the document is accompanied by a statement that the identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1067B deliver documents on their own behalf or on behalf of another as a disqualified person`
    `s 1085 inspect the register`
    `s 1086 require a copy of material on the register`
